<p class="sub">The book of Prosa carries the working title "Prose Under Law": it teaches the language to a writer who works with AI models. It lets a reader go from a first remark on a draft to a style the court keeps on every page.</p>
<!--main-->
<section>
  <div class="narrow">
    <h2>What the manuscript holds and how it is governed</h2>
    <p>The manuscript opens on a style held by a promise and on the reason it drifts back, then teaches the ten declarations one at a time. Its chapters are Markdown files, and a declaration, <code>book.proz</code>, binds them to the style of AYOUNI Press: the court of Prosa judges every chapter of the manuscript against the law the chapters teach.</p>
    <p>The chapters, their examples and the declaration stand in <a href="https://github.com/mayouni/prosa/tree/main/book">the folder of the book</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
